@startuml Sequence-Gerer-Incident-SOC
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor black
skinparam sequenceActorBorderColor black

title Diagramme de Séquence - Gérer un Incident SOC\n

actor "Admin SOC" as Admin
participant "Interface\nSOC" as UI
participant "Contrôleur\nIncidents" as Controller
participant "Service\nDétection" as Detective
participant "Service\nBlockage" as BlockService
participant "Base de\nDonnées" as DB

Admin -> UI: Accès /attacks (incidents)
UI -> Controller: GET /api/attacks
Controller -> DB: Récupérer tous les attacks
DB --> Controller: Liste des attacks
Controller --> UI: JSON (incidents, géo, status)
UI --> Admin: Affiche tableau incidents

Admin -> UI: Clique sur un incident
UI -> Controller: GET /api/attacks/{id}
Controller -> DB: Chercher attack par ID
DB --> Controller: Attack + commentaires + géo
Controller --> UI: Détails incident (JSON)
UI --> Admin: Affiche fiche incident

Admin -> UI: Change statut → "En cours"
UI -> Controller: PATCH /api/attacks/{id}/status
Controller -> DB: Mettre à jour attack.status
DB --> Controller: Status modifié
Controller --> UI: 200 OK
UI --> Admin: Affiche changement

Admin -> UI: Ajoute commentaire SOC
UI -> Controller: POST /api/attacks/{id}/comments
Controller -> DB: Créer AttackComment\n(user_id, comment, status)
DB --> Controller: Comment sauvegardé
Controller --> UI: 201 Created
UI --> Admin: Affiche commentaire

alt Décision: Bloquer IP source
    Admin -> UI: Clique "Bloquer IP"
    UI -> Controller: POST /api/blocked-ips
    
    Controller -> BlockService: bloquer IP source\n(source_ip, raison)
    BlockService -> DB: Enregistrer BlockedIP\n(ip, status='active', expires_at)
    DB --> BlockService: IP bloquée
    BlockService -> BlockService: Ajouter IP aux firewall rules
    
    BlockService --> Controller: IP bloquée avec succès
    Controller -> DB: Enregistrer action audit
    DB --> Controller: Audit enregistré
    Controller --> UI: 200 OK + "IP bloquée"
    UI --> Admin: Affiche confirmation

else Décision: Marquer investigation complète
    Admin -> UI: Change statut → "Résolu"
    UI -> Controller: PATCH /api/attacks/{id}/status
    Controller -> DB: status = 'resolved'
    DB --> Controller: Statut modifié
    Controller --> UI: 200 OK
    UI --> Admin: Incident fermé
end

Admin -> UI: Quitte la fiche
UI --> Admin: Retour à la liste

@enduml
